ically integrated supply chain"},"country":{"url":"https://www.ardian.com/news-insights/press-releases/ardian-signs-agreement-acquire-majority-stake-prosol-group","name":"Ardian","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2017-03-20","evidence":"Based in the Lyon region in France, Prosol, which is the cornerstone of the Grand Frais’ concept"},"employees":{"url":"https://www.ardian.com/news-insights/press-releases/ardian-announces-sale-its-stake-prosol-apollo","name":"Ardian","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2025-12-16","evidence":"the company employs nearly 10,000 people and operates across the country through nearly 450 stores in France"},"revenue":{"url":"https://www.ardian.com/news-insights/press-releases/ardian-announces-sale-its-stake-prosol-apollo","name":"Ardian","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2025-12-16","evidence":"The company generated revenues of more than €4.2 billion last year."},"business_model":{"url":"https://ir.apollo.com/news-events/press-releases/detail/623/apollo-funds-complete-acquisition-of-prosol-group","name":"Apollo Global Management","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-05-07","evidence":"Prosol operates and/or supplies nearly 450 stores across France under two main banners, Grand Frais and fresh."}},"holding":{"sponsor":"ARDIAN","status":"realized","status_note":"Majority stake acquired 2017 (agreement signed 20 March 2017); sold to Apollo Funds, completed May 2026","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"Buyout","value_creation_plan":"Ardian committed to providing all its resources to actively support the company and the Grand Frais brand in its ambitious growth strategy.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.ardian.com/news-insights/press-releases/ardian-signs-agreement-acquire-majority-stake-prosol-group","notes":"Ardian Mid Cap Buyout. During Ardian's ownership Prosol more than tripled revenue and acquired Océalliance (2022) and the Novoviande butcher network (2024). Batch listed this holding as current with 2026; Ardian's own release shows entry in 2017 and the sale to Apollo."}},{"name":"Nidec Components","website":"https://www.nidec-components.com/","description":"Nidec Components is an electronic components manufacturer that develops, manufactures, and sells industrial products including pressure sensors, switches, torque sensors and encoders.","sector":"Technology hardware","subsector":"Electronic components and sensors (switches, trimmer potentiometers, pressure sensors, encoders, precision motors, polygon mirrors)","country":"Japan","founded_year":1967,"business_model":"B2B manufacturing","employees":921,"employees_text":"Employees (Consolidated) 921 (As of March 31, 2025)","employees_as_of":"2025-03-31","revenue":32692000000,"revenue_currency":"JPY","revenue_period":"12 months to 2025-03-31","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Kazushi Ishida","title":"President","source_url":"https://www.nidec-components.com/file/company__company_guide/company_data_en.pdf","source_kind":"company","evidence":"President Kazushi ISHIDA"}],"notes":"Legal name Nidec Components Corporation; formerly Copal Electronics (est. 1967) and Nidec Copal Electronics (from 1999); renamed 2023; wholly owned by Nidec Corporation since 2014. Head office Nishi-Shinjuku Prime Square, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo. Nidec agreed on 1 Oct 2026 to sell all shares to TCG2603 Co., Ltd. (indirectly owned by a Carlyle fund); press reports put the transfer price at JPY 102.98 billion. Revenue and headcount from the company's own Company Data File (consolidated sales 32,692 million yen as of March 31, 2025).","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.carlyle.com/media-room/news-release-archive/carlyle-agrees-acquire-nidec-components","name":"Carlyle","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-10-01","evidence":"Founded in 1967, Nidec Components is an electronic components manufacturer that develops, manufactures, and sells a variety of industrial products including pressure sensors, switches, and torque sensors, encoders."},"founded_year":{"url":"https://www.nidec-components.com/file/company__company_guide/company_data_en.pdf","name":"Nidec Components","kind":"company","as_of":"2025-03-31","evidence":"Date of Foundation April 1, 1967"},"country":{"url":"https://www.nidec-components.com/file/company__company_guide/company_data_en.pdf","name":"Nidec Components","kind":"company","as_of":"2025-03-31","evidence":"Head Office Nishi-Shinjuku Prime Square Bldg., 7-5-25 Nishi-Shinjuku, Shinjuku-Ku, Tokyo 160-0023, JAPAN"},"employees":{"url":"https://www.nidec-components.com/file/company__company_guide/company_data_en.pdf","name":"Nidec Components","kind":"company","as_of":"2025-03-31","evidence":"Employees (Consolidated) 921 (As of March 31, 2025)"},"revenue":{"url":"https://www.nidec-components.com/file/company__company_guide/company_data_en.pdf","name":"Nidec Components","kind":"company","as_of":"2025-03-31","evidence":"Sales (Consolidated) 32,692 million yen (As of March 31, 2025)"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.carlyle.com/media-room/news-release-archive/carlyle-agrees-acquire-nidec-components","name":"Carlyle","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-10-01","evidence":"an electronic components manufacturer that develops, manufactures, and sells a variety of industrial products"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"The Carlyle Group","status_note":"Agreed 1 Oct 2026 to acquire 100% from Nidec Corporation; subject to regulatory approvals and closing conditions","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"Carve-out","value_creation_plan":"Working closely alongside management, Carlyle will support the future growth of the business, including through global expansion, operational improvement, and strengthening of the organizational structure, as an independent company with greater flexibility in decision-making, growth investment, and resource allocation.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.carlyle.com/media-room/news-release-archive/carlyle-agrees-acquire-nidec-components","notes":"Part of Nidec Corporation's portfolio rationalization. Buyer vehicle TCG2603 Co., Ltd. Carlyle cites prior Japan electronics investments (Rigaku, TOTOKU, Iwasaki Electric, Kyoden). Status left blank: agreement signed, closing pending."}},{"name":"Starcloud","website":"https://www.starcloud.com/","description":"Starcloud is building data centers in space to solve the AI energy bottleneck; it launched its first satellite, Starcloud-1, in November 2025 carrying the first NVIDIA H100 in orbit.","sector":"Space","subsector":"Orbital data centers / space-based AI compute","country":"United States","business_model":"B2B infrastructure (orbital compute and cloud workloads)","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Philip Johnston","title":"Co-Founder & CEO","source_url":"https://www.starcloud.com/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Meet our founders ... Philip Johnston | Co-Founder & CEO"},{"role":"other","name":"Ezra Feilden","title":"Co-Founder & CTO","source_url":"https://www.starcloud.com/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Ezra Feilden | Co-Founder & CTO"},{"role":"other","name":"Adi Oltean","title":"Co-Founder & Chief Engineer","source_url":"https://www.starcloud.com/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Adi Oltean | Co-Founder & Chief Engineer"}],"notes":"Starcloud, Inc., 2517 152nd Ave NE, Redmond, WA. $170M Series A at a $1.1B valuation (March 2026) in two tranches: Benchmark led the initial round with EQT Ventures participating, and both co-led an extension. No CFO, headcount or financials published; site prints no generic email.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://eqtgroup.com/about/current-portfolio/starcloud","name":"EQT","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Starcloud is building data centers in space to solve the AI energy bottleneck. Starcloud launched its first satellite, Starcloud-1, in November 2025. It featured the first NVIDIA H100 on board"},"country":{"url":"https://www.starcloud.com/","name":"Starcloud","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"© 2024 Starcloud, Inc. 2517 152nd Ave NE, Redmond, WA 98052"},"sector":{"url":"https://eqtgroup.com/about/current-portfolio/starcloud","name":"EQT","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Key Facts Sector Space Country United States Entry 2026"},"business_model":{"url":"https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/30/starcloud-raises-170-million-series-ato-build-data-centers-in-space/","name":"TechCrunch","kind":"press","as_of":"2026-03-30","evidence":"“There’s kind of two business models,” Johnston explains: One is selling processing power to other spacecraft on orbit"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"EQT AB","status":"current","status_note":"EQT Ventures co-led the $170M Series A (March 2026); EQT lists the company in its current portfolio with entry 2026","asset_class":"Venture capital","deal_type":"Venture round","value_creation_plan":"This funding round will support development on Starcloud-3 satellites, and allow the company to establish manufacturing capacity and increase headcount.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.satellitetoday.com/finance/2026/03/30/starcloud-raises-170m-to-fund-orbital-data-center-plans/","notes":"Round valued the company at $1.1 billion. Benchmark led the initial tranche with EQT Ventures participating; both co-led the extension. Other investors include NFX, Nebular and Y Combinator."}},{"name":"Tablet Command","website":"https://www.tabletcommand.com/","description":"Tablet Command provides real-time incident management and response software for fire departments and emergency response agencies, digitizing incident command workflows including tactical command, unit tracking, personnel accountability and post-incident reporting.","sector":"Technology","subsector":"Public safety / fire incident management software (GovTech)","country":"United States","founded_year":2011,"business_model":"B2G software","email":"info@tabletcommand.com","email_type":"generic","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"William Pigeon","title":"CEO & Co-Founder","source_url":"https://www.tabletcommand.com/our-team","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Leadership | William Pigeon | CEO & Co-Founder"},{"role":"other","name":"Andy Bozzo","title":"Co-Founder","source_url":"https://www.tabletcommand.com/our-team","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Andy Bozzo | Co-Founder"}],"notes":"HQ 1212 Broadway Plaza, Suite 2100, Walnut Creek, CA. TPG release (Sept 2026): serves more than 180 departments and agencies across the US and Canada including CAL FIRE, and about 28 of the largest US fire departments; the company's own boilerplate cites almost 80,000 users and more than 1,600 public safety agencies, and its team page says 1,500+ agencies and 62,000+ emergency responders. No CFO or headcount published.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.tpg.com/news-and-insights/tpg-to-make-significant-investment-in-tablet-command","name":"TPG","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-09-15","evidence":"Tablet Command provides real-time incident management software designed to help emergency response teams manage complex, time-sensitive operations. Its platform digitizes critical incident command workflows, including tactical command, unit tracking, personnel accountability, and post-incident reporting"},"founded_year":{"url":"https://www.tpg.com/news-and-insights/tpg-to-make-significant-investment-in-tablet-command","name":"TPG","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-09-15","evidence":"Founded in 2011 by Andy Bozzo and William Pigeon, Tablet Command provides real-time incident management software"},"country":{"url":"https://www.tabletcommand.com/contact_us","name":"Tablet Command","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"Tablet Command 1212 Broadway Plaza Suite 2100 Walnut Creek, CA 94596 United States"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.tpg.com/news-and-insights/tpg-to-make-significant-investment-in-tablet-command","name":"TPG","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-09-15","evidence":"providing critical technology to public safety agencies and first responders"},"email":{"url":"https://www.tabletcommand.com/contact_us","name":"Tablet Command","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"info@tabletcommand.com | All Inquiries: 877-998-2639"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"TPG","status_note":"The Rise Funds signed a definitive agreement (Sept 2026) to make a significant investment; expected to close in Q4 2026","asset_class":"Growth equity","deal_type":"Growth investment","value_creation_plan":"Partnership aimed to accelerate Tablet Command's continued growth and mission to equip fire departments and emergency response agencies with modern incident management technology; with TPG's resources the company will invest further in its team, technology and customers.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.tpg.com/news-and-insights/tpg-to-make-significant-investment-in-tablet-command","notes":"Made by The Rise Funds, TPG's multi-sector global impact investing strategy; builds on its climate adaptation and resilience focus. Status left blank: closing pending."}},{"name":"Alkermes","website":"https://www.alkermes.com/","description":"Alkermes plc is a global biopharmaceutical company focused on developing innovative medicines in the field of neuroscience.","sector":"Healthcare","subsector":"Biopharmaceuticals (neuroscience)","country":"Ireland","business_model":"B2B pharmaceutical (commercial products and royalties)","email":"investor_relations@alkermes.com","email_type":"investor_relations","employees":2050,"employees_text":"approximately 2,050 full time employees","employees_as_of":"2026-02-20","revenue":1475899000,"revenue_currency":"USD","revenue_period":"FY2025","ebitda":281121000,"ebitda_currency":"USD","ebitda_period":"FY2025","ebitda_basis":"derived","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Blair Jackson","title":"President & Chief Executive Officer","source_url":"https://www.alkermes.com/about-us/leadership","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Blair Jackson became President & Chief Executive Officer of Alkermes in August 2026."},{"role":"cfo","name":"Joshua Reed","title":"Senior Vice President, Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"http